{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned1", "translation": "a"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned2", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned3", "translation": "d"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned4", "translation": "turnings of the house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned5", "translation": "in bacchic rhythm"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned6", "translation": "turnings of the house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned7", "translation": "of the mind, he who to all"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned8", "translation": "n"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned9", "translation": "dear"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned10", "translation": "strophe"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned11", "translation": "antistrophe"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned12", "translation": "a"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned13", "translation": "strophe"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned14", "translation": "b"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-mentioned15", "translation": "d"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-quote1", "translation": "all-powerful, guileless, invincible king, godlike Darius, ruled the land"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-199-1-quote2", "translation": "he wishes this nearest bulwark of the Apian land, guarded by one man"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-comment1", "translation": "If the first words mean that all is well if Orestes is condemned, then ⟦1⟧ etc. connect poorly, since an \"otherwise\" is supplied only with difficulty. ⟦2⟧, however, must be the just punishment (on ⟦3⟧); clearly 799 ⟦4⟧ (see also ⟦5⟧). Thus we are led to the easy correction ⟦6⟧ for ⟦7⟧ (cf. 746 f.), so that the first words ⟦8⟧ . . ⟦9⟧ can mean: now a new justice is set in place of the old. Cf. Dante in Purgatorio I, 46 o è mutato in ciel nuovo consiglio; thus ⟦10⟧ (with Meineke) for ⟦11⟧. So ⟦12⟧ ⟦13⟧ (Paley)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned1", "translation": "all already"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned2", "translation": "Justice and harm"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned3", "translation": "so that Orestes, doing these things, suffers no harm"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned4", "translation": "or"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned5", "translation": "if"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned6", "translation": "now"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned7", "translation": "of ordinances"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned8", "translation": "turnings"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned9", "translation": "overthrowings"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-1-mentioned10", "translation": "to adapt new ways"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ also ⟦2⟧. To write ⟨⟦3⟧⟩ ⟦4⟧ (cf. ⟦5⟧ 485, etc.) is so easy that an irregular responsion of – ᴗ ᴗ – ᴗ ᴗ – and – ᴗ – ᴗ – ᴗ – need not be accepted here; cf. on 525."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-2-mentioned1", "translation": "Ordinance"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-2-mentioned2", "translation": "Te"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-2-mentioned3", "translation": "and"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-2-mentioned4", "translation": "testimonies and proofs"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-3-comment1", "translation": "With ⟦1⟧ one compares Plato Republic III, 391 E ⟦2⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-3-mentioned1", "translation": "facility"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-3-mentioned2", "translation": "lest they engender in the young much facility for wickedness"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (only here in Aeschylus) approximately \"accustom to\"."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-4-mentioned1", "translation": "will join together"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ i.e. ⟦2⟧ (Paley); ⟦3⟧ like ⟦4⟧ ⟦5⟧ ⟦6⟧ below 894, ⟦7⟧ \"await\" in Pindar, Sophocles and elsewhere, so that one need not correct with Weil to ⟦8⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-mentioned1", "translation": "True things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-mentioned2", "translation": "in deed and not in word"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-mentioned3", "translation": "awaits someone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-mentioned4", "translation": "possessions remain for descendants"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-mentioned5", "translation": "to await someone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-mentioned6", "translation": "will allot"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-5-quote1", "translation": "what honor remains for me"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-6-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ 478;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-6-mentioned1", "translation": "Afterwards"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-7-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧. 938 etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-200-7-mentioned1", "translation": "in time"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: as at 314. 943, at the second place without object; there is no compulsion for changes, apart from that of ⟦2⟧ to ⟦3⟧ (cf. ⟦4⟧ 508; ⟦5⟧, where M likewise has ⟦6⟧; ⟦7⟧ Casaubonus), since ⟦8⟧ can carry the two dependent genitives, Kühner-Gerth I, 337; ⟦9⟧' for ⟦10⟧ (Weil) is admittedly very close."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned1", "translation": "will creep upon"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned2", "translation": "neither"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned3", "translation": "nor"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned4", "translation": "nor"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned5", "translation": "neither"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned6", "translation": "not"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned7", "translation": "anger"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned8", "translation": "someone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-201-1-mentioned9", "translation": "someone"}]}